<?xml version='1.0'?>
<!--
  Federation for the hub-central baseline (deploy/docker/docker-compose.yml).

  Deliberately empty: this baseline names NO peer. That is the topology working as designed, not an
  omission. A joining baseline declares both directions itself (see hub-east/federation.xml), so an
  existing baseline is never edited, restarted, or redeployed when a new one appears (locked #44).

  What authorizes an incoming downstream command is the federation user's permissions in broker.xml's
  security-settings, which are identical in every baseline - so there is genuinely nothing peer-shaped
  to configure here.
-->
<federations xmlns="urn:activemq:core"/>
